<title>CHILE: Chile forex reserves climb to $15.95 bln.</title>
<headline>Chile forex reserves climb to $15.95 bln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's international reserves rose $227 million in the first two weeks of the month to total $15.95 billion on February 15, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>The rise was the result of a $241 million surplus in the balance of payments account and a $14 million fall in the value of the reserves due to international currency fluctuations.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
